description: Payment integrations and transaction safety
alwaysApply: false
globs: "apps/api/**/payment*/**/*.{ts,sql},apps/api/**/checkout/**/*.{ts,sql},apps/api/**/easypaisa/**/*.{ts,sql},apps/api/**/alfalah/**/*.{ts,sql}"
Payment Rules

Payment status must be determined by the backend.

Never trust a frontend success response.

Use a provider abstraction.

Conceptually:

PaymentProvider
├── EasyPaisaProvider
└── BankAlfalahProvider


Orders and checkout must not depend directly on provider-specific implementation details.

Payment operations must be idempotent.

Webhook/callback processing must safely handle duplicate delivery.

Store provider transaction identifiers.

Verify callbacks according to provider requirements.

Never expose provider secrets to frontend applications.

Never log payment credentials.

Payment states should be explicit.

Consider:

CREATED
PENDING
PROCESSING
SUCCESS
FAILED
EXPIRED
REFUNDED

Do not mark an order as paid merely because the customer returned from a payment page.

Server-side verification is mandatory.

Read docs/PAYMENTS.md before modifying payment behavior.